data: {"id":"chatcmpl-20261012152626622132038c955d568o4izCUI5","created":1791818787,"object":"chat.completion.chunk","model":"glm-5.3-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_8ffcd8240b2f47499a5e42fe","index":0,"type":"function","function":{"name":"file_write","arguments":"{\"content\":\"# MILP Formulation — Single-Vehicle Delivery Routing\\n\\nData source: `delivery_data.json`\\n\\n## 1. Optimization Purpose\\n\\nDecide the visiting order for one depot-based vehicle so that every customer\\n(A, B, C) receives its full demand, the vehicle's capacity is never exceeded,\\nand total travel distance is minimized.\\n\\n## 2. Sets & Parameters\\n\\n- Nodes: N = {D, A, B, C}; customers K = {A, B, C}; depot = D\\n- Demands q: q_A = 3, q_B = 4, q_C = 2 (total = 9)\\n- Capacity: Q = 6\\n- Distances d_ij (symmetric, d_ij = d_ji):\\n  D-A=5, D-B=8, D-C=6, A-B=4, A-C=7, B-C=3\\n\\n## 3. Decision Variables\\n\\n- x_ij ∈ {0, 1} for all ordered pairs i, j ∈ N, i ≠ j\\n  — 1 if the vehicle travels directly from i to j, else 0\\n- u_i (auxiliary, MTZ load variable) — cumulative load onboard after\\n  serving customer i\\n\\n## 4. Domains\\n\\n- x_ij ∈ {0, 1} (binary)\\n- q_i ≤ u_i ≤ Q (continuous, or integer)\\n\\n## 5. Constraints\\n\\n1. Each customer is entered exactly once:\\n   Σ_{h∈N, h≠i} x_hi = 1  ∀ i ∈ K\\n2. Each customer is left exactly once:\\n   Σ_{j∈N, j≠i} x_ij = 1  ∀ i ∈ K\\n3. Route starts and ends at the depot:\\n   Σ_{j∈K} x_Dj = 1  and  Σ_{h∈K} x_hD = 1\\n4. Subtour elimination + capacity (MTZ):\\n   u_j ≥ u_i + q_j − Q·(1 − x_ij)  ∀ i, j ∈ K, i ≠ j\\n\\n   This forbids disconnected customer-only subtours AND enforces that the\\n   onboard load never exceeds Q at any point on the route.\\n\\n## 6. Objective Function\\n\\nMinimize total travel distance:\\n\\n    Z = Σ_{i∈N} Σ_{j∈N, j≠i} d_ij · x_ij\\n\\n## 7. Assumptions\\n\\n1. Travel cost = distance; distances are symmetric and deterministic.\\n2. Service times, traffic, fuel, and time windows are ignored.\\n3. Each customer is served exactly once, full demand in one drop\\n   (no split deliveries).\\n4. The vehicle starts and ends at depot D.\\n\\n### Critical feasibility assumption\\n\\nTotal demand (3 + 4 + 2 = 9) EXCEEDS vehicle capacity (6). Under a strict\\nsingle-tour/no-reload interpretation the problem above is INFEASIBLE.\\n\\nAdopted assumption: the vehicle may return to D mid-route to reload\\n(multi-trip single vehicle). Capacity then applies per excursion, and\\nreloading at D is free/instant. Formally, the model gains a trip index\\nt ∈ {1..m}, m = ⌈Σq / Q⌉ = 2: variables x_ij^t, each customer assigned to\\nexactly one trip, depot degree = 1 in / 1 out per trip, MTZ per trip.\\n\\n### Consequences for this data set (verified by enumeration)\\n\\n- Unconstrained best single tour: D→A→B→C→D = 18 — but infeasible (load 9 > 6)\\n- Capacity-feasible optimum (2 trips): D→B→C→D then D→A→D = 17 + 10 = 27\\n  ({B,C} load exactly 6; then {A} load 3)\\n- Worst feasible option (3 solo trips): D→A→D + D→B→D + D→C→D = 38\\n\",\"path\":\"formulation.md\"}"}}]}}]}

